    <bpmn:process id="W_W4459" name="W4459. Safety-Sensitive &amp; Driver (LTFRB/DOTr) Role Identification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Policy (W4457); org/job change
Frequency: Annual + on role change
Volume: Safety-sensitive population (operators, drivers, chemical handlers) across 5 entities
Owner: HR (VS-103) / HSE (VS-24) / Fleet (VS-06)
Participants: HR (VS-103), HSE (VS-24), Fleet (VS-06), Store Ops (VS-07), Occupational Health (VS-83), Contingent (VS-98)
Source: workflow W4459 — Safety-Sensitive &amp; Driver (LTFRB/DOTr) Role Identification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4459_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4459_Lane1" name="HR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4459_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4459_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4459_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4459_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4459_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4459_Start3" name="Policy (W4457); org/job change">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4459_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4459_Task4" name="safety-sensitive">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: HR/HSE/Fleet identify &amp; classify safety-sensitive roles — powered-equipment operators (forklift/reach/order-picker), delivery drivers (LTFRB/DOTr-regulated), paint/chemical/hazmat handlers, equipment operators, security with firearm, and any role where impairment risks severe harm (links VS-147)
Responsible (R): HR / HSE / Fleet
Accountable (A): CHRO / HSE Lead
Duration: Annual + on change</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4459_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4459_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4459_Task5" name="HR/HSE set the testing-frequency/intensity per role class — safety-sensitive…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: HR/HSE set the testing-frequency/intensity per role class — safety-sensitive: random + post-incident + reasonable-suspicion + return-to-duty; non-safety-sensitive: pre-employment + reasonable-suspicion — per policy (W4457)
Responsible (R): HR / HSE
Accountable (A): CHRO / HSE Lead
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4459_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4459_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4459_Task6" name="HR/Fleet/Contingent flag safety-sensitive employees in HRIS, ensure…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: HR/Fleet/Contingent flag safety-sensitive employees in HRIS, ensure license/certification (LTFRB for drivers), and extend requirements to contingent/contractor (W4463)
Responsible (R): HR / Fleet / Contingent
Accountable (A): CHRO / Fleet Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4459_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4459_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4459_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4459_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4459_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-129 (ensure drug-free workplace program compliance.) | - CTL-680: safety-sensitive roles classified &amp; flagged; testing-frequency per class; driver license/cert tracked; contingent included (W4463)
Owner: HR (VS-103) / HSE (VS-24) / Fleet (VS-06)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4459_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4459_Annotation8" targetRef="W4459_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
